WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.160
Part 4 You will hear part of a presentation

00:00:04.160 --> 00:00:08.320
by a Tourism Studies student on the cruise ship industry.

00:00:09.920 --> 00:00:15.360
First, you have some time to look at questions 31 to 40.

00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:10.800
Now listen carefully and answer questions 31 to 40.

00:01:14.160 --> 00:01:19.519
For my presentation today, I'm going to talk about some of the issues facing the cruise ship

00:01:19.519 --> 00:01:26.160
industry, and then some ways these can be addressed. The cruise ship industry has partly

00:01:26.160 --> 00:01:33.360
been responsible for the effects of overtourism in recent decades. Overtourism occurs in places

00:01:33.360 --> 00:01:39.680
where excessive numbers of tourists cause significant problems. Pollution, for example,

00:01:39.680 --> 00:01:43.199
is among the greatest threats to many popular tourist destinations.

00:01:44.480 --> 00:01:48.320
Of course, for many places, it's a difficult balance to achieve.

00:01:49.199 --> 00:01:53.760
They want to promote their city or island as a desirable tourist destination,

00:01:54.400 --> 00:01:59.599
but at the same time are unable to cope with thousands of cruise ship passengers on a daily

00:01:59.599 --> 00:02:06.160
basis. The trouble is, excessive tourism is destroying the beauty spots and places of

00:02:06.160 --> 00:02:12.880
interest that people come to visit. Several cities, such as Barcelona, have responded by

00:02:12.880 --> 00:02:20.000
imposing a tax, which all visitors to the city from cruise ships have to pay. But as it's only

00:02:20.000 --> 00:02:25.679
a couple of euros, many green campaigners think it won't deter enough people to make any difference.

00:02:27.440 --> 00:02:33.360
Bruges is another city which became impossible to navigate at times because of the huge numbers

00:02:33.360 --> 00:02:40.240
of cruise passengers arriving on day trips from the port of Zeebrugge. The city was becoming like

00:02:40.240 --> 00:02:46.240
a theme park, with shops only catering for tourists selling chocolate, which Belgium is

00:02:46.240 --> 00:02:52.960
famous for, and other souvenirs. The local council took action to limit cruise passengers

00:02:52.960 --> 00:03:00.080
to a more manageable level. Dubrovnik had to limit the numbers of cruise ships after it became

00:03:00.080 --> 00:03:06.240
extremely popular as a cruise ship destination when it featured in a hugely successful TV series.

00:03:07.279 --> 00:03:12.479
What it does now is control the timing of all cruise ship entries to the city's port.

00:03:13.119 --> 00:03:16.960
However, many people feel this measure does not go far enough.

00:03:22.160 --> 00:03:27.759
Cruise ships may be unpopular in some of their destinations, but they also have an image problem.

00:03:28.559 --> 00:03:34.559
They've always been perceived as a safe holiday for the elderly, with not much on offer for families

00:03:34.559 --> 00:03:42.080
or young couples. A recent survey showed that cost is also a major factor in putting younger

00:03:42.080 --> 00:03:48.399
groups off going on a cruise. But what they don't realize is that compared to other types of package

00:03:48.399 --> 00:03:55.440
holidays, cruises can actually be good value, as all activities and drinks are often included.

00:03:56.160 --> 00:04:01.839
And another perception is that cruises have lots of rules about what to wear and how to behave.

00:04:02.639 --> 00:04:07.919
But these days, most cruises are no longer very formal and behind the times.

00:04:08.880 --> 00:04:13.119
So what solutions are there for cruise lines to overcome some of these problems?

00:04:14.000 --> 00:04:20.720
How can they appeal to younger customers? Well, one selling point is that cruise ships are becoming

00:04:20.720 --> 00:04:28.399
more sustainable. New ships are built with hybrid engines with large batteries, which means ships do

00:04:28.399 --> 00:04:34.399
not have to keep their engines running while docked. Cruise lines are also designing ships

00:04:34.559 --> 00:04:42.799
specially for those in the age range of 21 to 45. The decor in these feels contemporary,

00:04:42.799 --> 00:04:47.839
and there are a range of activities on board that you wouldn't find on a more traditional cruise.

00:04:48.480 --> 00:04:54.799
There's even a boxing ring on one ship, and most offer diving expeditions. But there's also a huge

00:04:54.799 --> 00:05:03.200
focus on well-being, with a variety of sessions of different kinds. Food is always a very important

00:05:03.200 --> 00:05:09.119
part of any cruise, and cruise ships have had to radically update their menus to suit the tastes

00:05:09.119 --> 00:05:15.760
of their younger customers. Vegan dishes are standard, for example. The restaurants on board

00:05:15.760 --> 00:05:24.000
have also gone paperless, with menus available on screen. Unlike older generations who went on

00:05:24.000 --> 00:05:29.359
cruises largely to get away from everything, younger people expect to be able to keep in

00:05:29.359 --> 00:05:35.440
touch with friends and family. Many people going on longer cruises also spend time working,

00:05:36.000 --> 00:05:40.640
so companies have to guarantee Wi-Fi that can be relied upon at all times.

00:05:42.079 --> 00:05:46.880
My grandparents used to love looking through cruise brochures, even when they weren't planning

00:05:46.880 --> 00:05:53.679
on going on a cruise. Until very recently, TV ads for cruises always felt dated and aimed at

00:05:53.679 --> 00:06:01.119
retirees. Cruise lines have been slowed to adopt the power of social media, but that's all changing.

00:06:02.000 --> 00:06:07.279
Leading cruise lines now employ top agencies to produce first-rate videos

00:06:07.279 --> 00:06:12.239
for social media channels. It will be interesting to see whether the cruise...

00:06:23.679 --> 00:06:24.320
you

